      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Even though Bell's palsy primarily affects facial movement, some symptoms can be asymmetric or involve other areas. Since you've been experiencing no numbness, weakness, or other systemic symptoms, it's still a good idea to consult your doctor to rule out any other underlying causes. Your doctor might want to perform a neurological exam or refer you for further evaluation, but ER visits can often be avoided with a simple doctor's visit.",
      "source": "target",
