      "content": "While vitamins and supplements can't hurt, there's no proven evidence that specific supplements can accelerate recovery from Bell's palsy. That being said, some studies suggest that taking vitamin B6 and supplementing with omega-3 fatty acids may help alleviate symptoms, but these are not a replacement for medical advice. Herbal remedies like ginger and turmeric may also have anti-inflammatory properties, but their effectiveness is largely anecdotal.",
